<title>USA: Archer Daniels to plead guilty in price-fix case.</title>
<headline>Archer Daniels to plead guilty in price-fix case.</headline>
<dateline>DECATUR, Ill. 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Archer Daniels Midland Co. said Monday it agreed to plead guilty to federal charges related to price-fixing and pay fines totalling $100 million.</p>
<p>ADM said the agreement, which is subject to court approval, settles the Justice Department's investigation of price-fixing of feed additive lysine and citric acid, and closes a third investigation related to high-fructose corn syrup.</p>
</text>
